From ff0b3ab6f8e14f1b38e21f2481554fa48c204437 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rebelancap <7285817+rebelancap@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:19:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] openxr: mobile OpenGL ES path (port of QuestCraft
 DeviceCompat.Mobile)

Upstream's DeviceCompat.Mobile has its GLES code commented out because
stock LWJGL 3.4.1 lwjgl-openxr ships no XR_KHR_opengl_es_enable /
XR_KHR_android_create_instance / XR_KHR_loader_init_android bindings
(QuestCraft used a custom LWJGL build). Port QuestCraft's working
implementation onto upstream's interface, writing the five structs by
hand from the Khronos openxr.h layouts and calling
xrGetOpenGLESGraphicsRequirementsKHR through xrGetInstanceProcAddr +
JNI.callPJPI (the same call LWJGL's generated KHROpenGLEnable makes).

- DeviceCompat.mobileRequested(): -Dvivecraft.openxr.mobile=true|false
  wins when set, else os.version contains "Android" (QuestCraft rule).
- Mobile: xrInitializeLoaderKHR(XrLoaderInitInfoAndroidKHR),
  XrInstanceCreateInfoAndroidKHR on the instance chain, GLES graphics
  requirements before xrCreateSession, XrGraphicsBindingOpenGLESAndroidKHR
  from VLoader's EGL handles, swapchain images typed
  XR_TYPE_SWAPCHAIN_IMAGE_OPENGL_ES_KHR. Vulkan is refused with a message.
- QuestCraft's 2.5 s loader delay is opt-in:
  -Dvivecraft.openxr.mobile.loaderDelayMs=2500.
- VRSettings: default stereo provider is OPENXR on the mobile path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
